# Example requests for the campaigns API (FR-1, FR-2), for the VS Code REST Client extension.
# Start the API with `pnpm dev` and seed the database first (`pnpm db:seed`).
# The API listens on 127.0.0.1 only (ADR-0003).

@base = http://127.0.0.1:4000

### Create a campaign: 4 dental search terms × 2 areas = 8 searches
# @name created
POST {{base}}/campaigns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nicheSlug": "dental-clinic",
  "city": "Lahore",
  "areas": ["DHA", "Gulberg"]
}

### List campaigns, newest first
GET {{base}}/campaigns

### Get the campaign created above
GET {{base}}/campaigns/{{created.response.body.id}}

### 400: no areas, with the Zod message per field
POST {{base}}/campaigns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nicheSlug": "dental-clinic",
  "city": "Lahore",
  "areas": []
}

### 404: unknown niche
POST {{base}}/campaigns
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nicheSlug": "bakery",
  "city": "Lahore",
  "areas": ["DHA"]
}
